      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Replacing a by 23 in the expression a + 3, we get, s = 23 + 3 = 26 years. Letters such as a and s that are used to represent numbers are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "letter-numbers",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Mathematical expressions containing letter-numbers, such as the expression a + 3, are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "algebraic expressions",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.171,
            0.808,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Given the age of Shabnam, write an expression to find Aftab’s age."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.203,
            0.848,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that Aftab is 3 years younger than Shabnam. So, Aftab’s age will be 3 less than Shabnam’s. This can be described as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.381,
            0.245,
            0.701,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Aftab’s age = Shabnam’s age – 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.269,
            0.849,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we again use the letter a to denote Aftab’s age and the letter s to denote Shabnam’s age, then the algebraic expression would be: a = s – 3, meaning 3 less than s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.334,
            0.755,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Use this expression to find Aftab’s age if Shabnam’s age is 20."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.375,
            0.848,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Parthiv is making matchstick patterns. He repeatedly places Ls next to each other. Each L has two matchsticks as shown in Figure 4.2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.448,
            0.843,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.155,
                0.448,
                0.843,
                0.536
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.468,
                0.541,
                0.534,
                0.556
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 4.2"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.568,
            0.846,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many matchsticks are needed to make 5 Ls? It will be 5 × 2. How many matchsticks are needed to make 7 Ls? It will be 7 × 2. How many matchsticks are needed to make 45 Ls? It will be 45 × 2. Now, what is the relation between the number of Ls and the number of sticks?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.661,
            0.848,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "First, let us describe the relationship or the pattern here. Every L needs 2 matchsticks. So "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the number of matchsticks needed will be 2 times the number of L’s",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". This can be written as:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.283,
            0.721,
            0.715,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Number of matchsticks = 2 × Number of L’s"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.746,
            0.846,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, we can use any letter to denote the number of L’s. Let’s use n. The algebraic expression for the number of matchsticks will be:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.469,
            0.788,
            0.528,
            0.806
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "2 \\times n ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.812,
            0.848,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This expression tells us how many matchsticks are needed to make n L’s. To find the number of matchsticks, we just replace n by the number of L."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.877,
            0.847,
            0.918
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 3:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Ketaki prepares and supplies coconut-jaggery laddus. The price of a coconut is ₹35 and the price of 1 kg jaggery is ₹60."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
